# Task 5: Average Order Value (AOV) Over Time — Monthly Trend

## Objective

The objective of this task is to analyze how the Average Order Value (AOV) changes month over month in 2022.

## Formula Used

AOV = SUM(after_discount) / COUNT(DISTINCT order_id)

## Tools Used

- Python
- Pandas
- SQLite
- SQL
- VS Code
- Google Looker Studio

## Dataset Features Used

- order_date
- after_discount
- order_id

## Steps Performed

1. Loaded order data into SQLite
2. Filtered data for the year 2022
3. Grouped data by month
4. Calculated total revenue
5. Counted distinct orders
6. Calculated AOV
7. Exported results to CSV
8. Created a line chart in Looker Studio

## Output File

monthly_aov_2022.csv

## Visualization

Line chart showing the monthly AOV trend for 2022.
LInk: https://datastudio.google.com/reporting/76ffad18-b3b7-4a27-ae09-cffbf301e204

## Business Insight

This analysis helps the sales team understand customer spending behavior and identify seasonal purchasing patterns.
